# Standard Example
A majority of the types listed will be obtained from a swagger file maintained externally by the backend team. 
[swagger-user](../../../../src/_shared/types/swagger-user.ts) - for user portal apis (most commonly used)
[swagger-sap](../../../../src/_shared/types/swagger-sap.ts) - for SuperAdmin portal apis
[swagger-starrocks](../../../../src/_shared/types/swagger-starrocks.ts) - for starrocks features

## Generated types vs runtime API

OpenAPI/Swagger unions and enums sometimes **lag** the live API. If the backend accepts a string value that is **not yet** in the generated TypeScript union, you may use a **narrow assertion** (e.g. `as ResourceAndAccessType`) **only** when the value is confirmed valid for the API, and prefer fixing the spec/generator long term. Do not change runtime request shapes just to satisfy outdated types.

## Response types and UI-only fields

- When the BE adds fields the UI needs but swagger is late, extend the **response interface** with **optional** properties (e.g. `password?`, `attuUrl?`) so call sites use **`?.`** instead of unsafe casts.
- **Request body** types must match the real **HTTP method** and payload (**PUT** vs **POST**, field names). Keep section comments in the types file aligned with the service function they pair with—reviewers should not have to guess.

## Enums for API-facing values

- Prefer **`E`-prefixed enums** for values sent to the API (metric ranges, status filters, etc.) instead of string literals in stores and services, so defaults and resets stay type-safe.

When adding new types to the .ts files, 
1.  Types and interfaces **MUST** start with an "I" prefix
    Examples from [kafka](../../src/types/project-management/kafka.ts): **I**ConsumerGrp, **I**ConsumerGrpFilter

2.  Enumerations **MUST** start with an "E" prefix
    Examples from [hbase](../../src/types/project-management/hbase.ts): **E**ProjectHBaseTableType, **E**ProjectHBaseEnv

When specifying types for a feature, use comments to create blocks to make it easier to find which type corresponds to which feature, for example
[kafka](../../src/types/project-management/kafka.ts)
```ts
// Topic and Quota Subtab Start

// Table Start
export type IKakfaTopicAndQuotaDetail = components['schemas']['KafkaBigdataAccountTopicVo'];
// Table End

// Topic and Quota Subtab End
```
